Never take OVMF's IGVM parameter area: no memory map and no vCPU count
from it, whatever bytes are at 0x812000.

Our own patch, on top of upstream's 0004, which stays. Upstream will
never carry it: it is right only where no IGVM loader runs. This project
boots OVMF under QEMU 8.2.2, which has no IGVM loader at all
(`qemu-system-x86_64 -object help` lists no igvm-cfg), and the plugin
never passes one. So the area at PcdOvmfIgvmParamBase can hold nothing
but what was in RAM before a reset.

Why 0004 is not enough (docs/decisions/0018): 0004 reserves the page, so
an OS that honours the firmware's memory map leaves it zero, as 10.9
does. 10.6 does not get the choice. Its kernel sits at fixed low
physical memory, and OpenCore's relocation block copies it there at
ExitBootServices, over whatever the firmware reserved. Under 10.6 the
page holds the kernel's own bytes, and whether a warm restart hangs
depends on the kernel build. 10.6.8's happens to be safe.

What it changes: mIgvmParamsInvalid starts TRUE instead of FALSE.
PlatformIgvmMemoryMapFind and PlatformIgvmVpCount, the only two readers
of the parameter area, test that flag before they read anything, and
nothing sets it back to FALSE. So the memory map check reports no map,
and E820 comes from fw_cfg's etc/e820. The vCPU count reports none, so
PlatformMaxCpuCountInitialization asks fw_cfg and the CPU-hotplug block.
That is exactly what a cold boot already did with a zeroed page. One
line, in the one file that reads the area. Rejected: setting
PcdOvmfIgvmParamBase to 0. That PCD is assigned by the MEMFD region in
OvmfPkg/Include/Fdf/MemFd.fdf.inc, which the reset vector's IGVM
metadata also describes, so it would move the firmware's memory layout
to change one decision.

Not changed: PlatformIgvmDataHobs, which walks the separate IGVM data-HOB
page at PcdOvmfIgvmHobBase (0x813000). It takes an entry only when its
type is a GUID extension and its 16-byte GUID is gEfiIgvmDataHobGuid,
which leftover RAM does not match in practice.

Applied by internal/firmware's OVMF build after 0004, unless Igvm.c
already carries this file's marker comment. Its hunk keeps upstream's
CRLF line endings.

diff --git a/OvmfPkg/Library/PlatformInitLib/Igvm.c b/OvmfPkg/Library/PlatformInitLib/Igvm.c
--- a/OvmfPkg/Library/PlatformInitLib/Igvm.c
+++ b/OvmfPkg/Library/PlatformInitLib/Igvm.c
@@ -36,7 +36,12 @@ typedef struct IGVM_MEMORY_MAP_ENTRY {
   UINT32    Reserved;
 } IGVM_MEMORY_MAP_ENTRY;
 
-STATIC BOOLEAN  mIgvmParamsInvalid;
+//
+// packer-plugin-macosx: assets/firmware/patches/0005-ovmf-never-read-igvm-parameters.patch
+// QEMU never loads an IGVM file here, so the parameter area holds no
+// parameters, only what was in RAM before a reset: never take it.
+//
+STATIC BOOLEAN  mIgvmParamsInvalid = TRUE;
 
 STATIC
 IGVM_MEMORY_MAP_ENTRY *
